.TH CAIRN 1 "2026-11-20" "Cairn 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cairn \- a file manager for Ubuntu that keeps folders tidy
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cairn
[\fB\-\-new\-window\fR | \fB\-\-new\-workspace\fR | \fB\-\-free\-up\-space\fR]
[\fIFOLDER\-OR\-FILE\fR...]
.br
.B cairn
.I COMMAND
[\fIARGUMENT\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Cairn browses your files and keeps folders tidy. It shows a plan before
anything moves, and one Undo puts everything back.
.PP
Cairn runs once per session. Starting it again hands the request to the
window that is already open.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I FOLDER\-OR\-FILE
Open a folder; for a file, open its folder with the file selected.
.TP
.B \-\-new\-window
Bring the window forward, showing the Home folder.
.TP
.B \-\-new\-workspace
Ask for the name of a new workspace.
.TP
.B \-\-free\-up\-space
Open Free Up Space.
.TP
.BR \-\-help ", " \-\-version
Print the commands, or the version, and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI open " PATH" ...
Open a folder, or a file's folder with the file selected.
.TP
.BI open\-workspace " NAME"
Open a workspace by its name, or by its place in the sidebar (#1 to #9).
Quote a name that has spaces.
.TP
.BR new\-workspace " [\fINAME\fR]"
Make a workspace with that name; without a name, ask for one.
.TP
.BI add\-link " URL"
Save a link to Bookmarks. Its title and picture are fetched from the
link's site unless that is turned off in Preferences.
.TP
.B free\-up\-space
Open Free Up Space.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/cairn/app.db
Workspaces, bookmarks, sidebar order and the undo journal.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/cairn/
The search index and other caches; safe to delete.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nautilus (1)
